1
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:04,433
Even after we graduate,

2
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,767
could we still meet up once in a while?

3
00:00:12,767 --> 00:00:13,767
Sure, I don't mind.

4
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,633
It's only meeting up.

5
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:22,067
Yes!

6
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:28,267
Right up to the end,

7
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,933
what Midori really thought of me

8
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:32,100
was something I never knew.

9
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:40,233
first year at university.

10
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:55,733
Sorry to keep you waiting, Midori.

11
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:57,433
Hey.

12
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:00,300
Did you change your hairstyle, Midori?

13
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,533
Good eye.

14
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:05,266
It really suits you, with your forehead showing.

15
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:07,467
Thanks, I guess.

16
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:13,567
- Welcome in.
- Thanks.

17
00:01:15,433 --> 00:01:17,233
Sorry for inviting you so suddenly.

18
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:18,867
Not at all.

19
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:22,267
Third period got cancelled today because of the professor.

20
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:26,633
- You never ended up joining a club, Hayama?
- No.

21
00:01:27,267 --> 00:01:29,233
You're in the track club, right, Midori?

22
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:33,167
Yeah, though I'm not as serious about it as in high school.

23
00:01:33,167 --> 00:01:38,067
Your last meet was so cool.

24
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,133
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

25
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:44,133
It wasn't that long ago, but it feels nostalgic.

26
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:47,633
I guess I've gotten used to university life already.

27
00:01:49,133 --> 00:01:50,333
Yeah, I guess so.

28
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:55,833
That's why I'm happy I can still see you like this, Midori.

29
00:02:00,067 --> 00:02:03,933
I mean, I'm glad to see a friend from high school.

30
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,500
A friend.

31
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:10,733
You know, we end up not seeing each other much.

32
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,467
Yeah, true.

33
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:18,767
Oh, I think I'll get the pudding today.

34
00:02:19,767 --> 00:02:21,000
You mean again today.

35
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:24,067
Huh? Did I order pudding last time too?

36
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:27,100
You always order it when we eat together.

37
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:30,967
Don't tell me you didn't even realize.

38
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:33,833
Yeah. I like pudding.

39
00:02:34,967 --> 00:02:36,233
I really didn't realize.

40
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,733
Seriously?

41
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:42,667
Then I'll have...

42
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:45,600
Hmm, napolitan sounds good too.

43
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,200
And garlic rice is hard to pass up.

44
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:53,633
So the other day, a senior at my university said

45
00:02:53,633 --> 00:02:55,767
that when everyone's making a toast,

46
00:02:55,767 --> 00:02:57,233
if you wave your glass like a wiper,

47
00:02:57,233 --> 00:03:00,267
- it counts as toasting people far away too.
- What's that?

48
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:02,500
Huh? Don't you do that at your university, Midori?

49
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,167
- Never heard of it.
- Huh?

50
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:07,067
- Maybe you just don't know about it, Midori.
- Huh?

51
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,933
Well, I'll invite you again if something comes up.

52
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:13,933
Thanks.

53
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,833
If he's inviting me,

54
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:28,100
does that mean he thinks of me as a friend?

55
00:03:44,033 --> 00:03:45,200
A friend, huh.

56
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:19,300
♪

57
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,600
♪

58
00:04:24,133 --> 00:04:27,267
♪

59
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,367
♪

60
00:04:34,233 --> 00:04:35,900
I barely made it to attendance.

61
00:04:36,433 --> 00:04:39,733
- Thanks, you saved me.
- If I hadn't woken you up with a call,

62
00:04:39,733 --> 00:04:41,467
you'd have failed that required course by now, Iida.

63
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:43,367
You're absolutely right.

64
00:04:43,367 --> 00:04:45,833
I won't forget this favor for a week.

65
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:47,733
Remember it for life!

66
00:04:48,567 --> 00:04:52,033
A week! And I'm counting on you next week too!

67
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,767
If you're that bad with mornings,

68
00:04:53,767 --> 00:04:55,367
get your girlfriend to wake you up.

69
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,300
Well, we broke up the other day.

70
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:01,133
That was fast. You already broke up?

71
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:03,133
There's no point staying with someone you don't click with.

72
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:04,300
It's a waste of time.

73
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:06,367
Well, that's true, but...

74
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,700
you just move on too fast.

75
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,667
I came up through the school, so I know a lot of people.

76
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:13,133
- I'll introduce you to a nice girl too, Yamamura.
- What?

77
00:05:13,967 --> 00:05:16,333
No, it's fine. I appreciate the thought.

78
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:21,233
- If you're thanking me, make it something tangible.
- Yamamura, you don't have a girlfriend now, ri

79
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,100
I don't, but...

80
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,100
Is there someone you like?

81
00:05:31,733 --> 00:05:33,867
It's not really like that.

82
00:05:33,867 --> 00:05:35,767
Then there's no problem.

83
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:41,033
Actually, there's a girl who says she's interested in you.

84
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:45,967
I already sent you her contact info.

85
00:05:46,633 --> 00:05:47,433
I said no thanks.

86
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
You're weird. Most people wouldn't resist this much.

87
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,533
Why are you refusing so hard?

88
00:05:59,267 --> 00:06:00,433
Fine.

89
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,433
I'll meet her.

90
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:13,467
So you're still meeting up with Yamamura.

91
00:06:13,867 --> 00:06:14,367
Yeah.

92
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:16,167
But...

93
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,333
Midori and I,

94
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,867
what are we, exactly?

95
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:24,767
Well, he probably thinks of you as a friend.

96
00:06:26,167 --> 00:06:26,867
You think so?

97
00:06:28,133 --> 00:06:29,800
If that's the case, I guess it's fine.

98
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,267
Is it?

99
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:36,733
You want to be more than friends, don't you, Ao?

100
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:41,900
Well, yes, but...

101
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:47,433
- But I don't want to ask for too much.
- Why?

102
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,033
Because...

103
00:06:58,567 --> 00:06:59,767
What about how you feel, Ao?

104
00:07:01,167 --> 00:07:02,133
Well?

105
00:07:07,233 --> 00:07:10,467
Right now, just being with Midori is enough for me.

106
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:15,000
Hmm.

107
00:07:34,933 --> 00:07:35,433
Um...

108
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,833
I'm Minami.

109
00:07:41,367 --> 00:07:44,900
Did Iida pass my contact info on to you?

110
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,067
Oh, yes, he did.

111
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:50,567
I'm Yamamura Midori.

112
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,867
Sorry, Yamamura.

113
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:59,167
I wondered if I made Iida pass it on to you against his will.

114
00:07:59,167 --> 00:08:01,233
No, not at all.

115
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,233
That's a relief.

116
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:06,800
Oh,

117
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,667
I'm in the same PE class as you.

118
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:12,500
That's how I knew who you were.

119
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,300
Oh, I see.

120
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,633
I noticed someone who runs really beautifully,

121
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:25,700
so I'm glad we've gotten to know each other.

122
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:29,533
Nice to meet you, Yamamura.

123
00:08:31,967 --> 00:08:32,467
Nice to meet you too.

124
00:08:35,232 --> 00:08:37,600
No, I'm doing it. I really am.

125
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,033
Wait, you're already done?

126
00:08:39,366 --> 00:08:41,700
- I'm done too.
- Wow, impressive.

127
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,000
So, how's it going with Minami?

128
00:08:46,133 --> 00:08:48,400
I've seen you two talking quite a bit.

129
00:08:49,267 --> 00:08:51,700
What do you mean? It's nothing.

130
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
She's a nice girl, isn't she?

131
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:01,867
Yeah, she's definitely nice. She's gentle, too.

132
00:09:01,867 --> 00:09:03,300
I think you two would get along.

133
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:05,100
You think?

134
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:09,600
If you're up for it, I bet it'd happen fast.

135
00:09:09,733 --> 00:09:13,233
Let me know if it works out.

136
00:09:20,533 --> 00:09:22,233
Oh, Iida.

137
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,167
Ao.

138
00:09:51,233 --> 00:09:52,600
What are you doing?

139
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,367
Basking in the sun.

140
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:57,100
It feels nice today.

141
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:01,233
It really does.

142
00:10:05,567 --> 00:10:08,400
Hey, let's go get tea right now.

143
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:11,067
But we have class next.

144
00:10:11,067 --> 00:10:13,400
It's fine. They don't take attendance in that class.

145
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:16,667
I want to be with you, Ao.

146
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:23,367
You know, I like you, Ao.

147
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,933
I'm sorry.

148
00:10:36,467 --> 00:10:37,867
I have someone I like.

149
00:10:38,733 --> 00:10:40,533
I like that person a lot.

150
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:44,267
So I can't return your feelings, Imai.

151
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:47,400
Huh?

152
00:10:49,167 --> 00:10:50,700
No, I... even so,

153
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:55,233
Besides, I don't plan on getting a girlfriend.

154
00:10:56,767 --> 00:10:57,967
I'm sorry.

155
00:11:00,533 --> 00:11:01,033
Huh?

156
00:11:04,633 --> 00:11:07,433
You know, Ao, you get popular as long as you keep quiet.

157
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:09,500
What do you mean, "as long as I keep quiet"?

158
00:11:10,267 --> 00:11:13,733
That's the third person to confess to you since you started uni, isn't it?

159
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,567
But with the person I really like, I'm getting nowhere.

160
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:24,233
He hasn't even messaged me about meals lately.

161
00:11:28,067 --> 00:11:30,133
Can you afford to sit there sulking?

162
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:34,500
You said you wanted to keep things as they are, Ao.

163
00:11:35,733 --> 00:11:37,767
But Yamamura must be popular too, right?

164
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:43,167
True. He's so good-looking, after all.

165
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:49,667
You're at different universities now, so you can't afford to be so laid-back.

166
00:11:53,267 --> 00:11:55,433
There's no use regretting it afterward, right?

167
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,400
Yamamura.

168
00:12:12,133 --> 00:12:12,633
Yeah?

169
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:14,767
Thanks for the notes.

170
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:15,833
Sure.

171
00:12:16,267 --> 00:12:19,033
Your notes are so neat, Yamamura, so they were easy to follow.

172
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:20,900
Really?

173
00:12:20,933 --> 00:12:22,267
Glad to hear it.

174
00:12:24,033 --> 00:12:25,667
Let me thank you somehow.

175
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,000
You don't need to.

176
00:12:29,767 --> 00:12:31,467
But you really helped me out.

177
00:12:32,133 --> 00:12:35,367
If you're free, do you want to go out together next Sunday?

178
00:12:38,867 --> 00:12:39,367
Huh?

179
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:46,567
Of course, part of it is wanting to thank you,

180
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:54,167
but I also want to get closer to you, Yamamura.

181
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:05,033
Going out with this girl

182
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:08,600
might be an option.

183
00:13:12,767 --> 00:13:19,400
Then maybe I could be happy in an ordinary way.

184
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:34,367
Do you want to get a meal next Sunday?

185
00:13:43,067 --> 00:13:43,700
What's wrong?

186
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:48,367
Oh, it's from a high school classmate.

187
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:53,733
Wow, he still contacts you after graduation. He must be a good friend.

188
00:13:58,667 --> 00:13:59,633
A friend.

189
00:14:02,433 --> 00:14:04,133
He's a friend, right?

190
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:20,633
Midori!

191
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:22,933
Hey.

192
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:30,867
What?

193
00:14:31,967 --> 00:14:34,967
No, it's just... are you really that happy to see me?

194
00:14:35,433 --> 00:14:35,933
Yeah.

195
00:14:42,733 --> 00:14:44,667
It feels like it's been a while.

196
00:14:45,833 --> 00:14:48,433
Yeah. Have you been busy?

197
00:14:49,633 --> 00:14:51,167
Kind of, yeah.

198
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:55,800
I was wondering what you were up to, Midori.

199
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:00,433
Oh, I mean, well...

200
00:15:01,533 --> 00:15:04,667
It's because you're happy to see a friend, right?

201
00:15:06,233 --> 00:15:07,667
Well, yes, but...

202
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,067
What are you having?

203
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:12,067
Oh, omurice.

204
00:15:13,067 --> 00:15:15,767
You love eggs, huh.

205
00:15:16,667 --> 00:15:17,633
Huh? How do you know?

206
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:19,567
Come on, it's obvious.

207
00:15:29,833 --> 00:15:33,067
Are there a lot of girls in your department, Midori?

208
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:35,167
Hmm, about half and half.

209
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:36,667
Oh, I see.

210
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:39,333
Mine has more guys.

211
00:15:39,733 --> 00:15:41,333
That's because you're in computer science.

212
00:15:45,667 --> 00:15:47,167
Have you made any friends?

213
00:15:50,833 --> 00:15:51,967
Um, well,

214
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:53,933
both guys and girls,

215
00:15:55,533 --> 00:15:57,100
I've made friends like normal.

216
00:16:02,033 --> 00:16:03,500
Um, is there anyone you're close to?

217
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:16,867
Anyway, we can't do anything until we know if Yamamura is single.

218
00:16:17,333 --> 00:16:19,000
Make sure you ask him properly.

219
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,833
Ugh, can I even ask that well?

220
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:28,033
I can't ask it smoothly at all.

221
00:16:29,633 --> 00:16:32,533
Well, I'm pretty close with Iida.

222
00:16:33,267 --> 00:16:34,400
He's a weirdo, though.

223
00:16:34,933 --> 00:16:35,600
I see.

224
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:42,667
Other than him, there aren't many girls.

225
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:49,933
True, you didn't talk to girls much in high school either, Midori.

226
00:16:55,367 --> 00:16:57,900
But there's one I've gotten close to lately.

227
00:17:02,267 --> 00:17:03,500
Are you close?

228
00:17:07,133 --> 00:17:10,467
Closer than with the others, yeah.

229
00:17:13,233 --> 00:17:14,000
What's she like?

230
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,900
What do you mean, what's she like?

231
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:23,200
She's gentle and soft-spoken, and kind. A good person.

232
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:29,633
I see.

233
00:17:31,933 --> 00:17:33,367
If she's a good person, that's great.

234
00:17:36,967 --> 00:17:37,767
Great?

235
00:17:39,567 --> 00:17:40,067
Yeah.

236
00:17:53,433 --> 00:17:54,600
Hayama,

237
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:56,400
Yeah?

238
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:01,400
aren't you going to get a girlfriend?

239
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,233
You must be popular. You can do everything.

240
00:18:11,033 --> 00:18:14,833
I'm not going to get a girlfriend.

241
00:18:17,867 --> 00:18:18,767
Why not?

242
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:22,767
Because I don't need one.

243
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:35,067
- Normal people want one. You're weird.
- I'm not weird.

244
00:18:39,767 --> 00:18:40,667
I'm not weird.

245
00:18:43,267 --> 00:18:45,067
There's nothing weird about it.

246
00:18:56,933 --> 00:18:57,533
I see.

247
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,500
See you again. Meeting you, Midori...

248
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:26,300
It's not because I'm meeting a friend.

249
00:19:29,467 --> 00:19:30,867
It's because I get to see you, Midori.

250
00:19:32,767 --> 00:19:34,133
That's why I was happy.

251
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:44,867
Bye.

252
00:19:47,133 --> 00:19:47,900
Thanks for meeting me.

253
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:18,700
There's nothing weird about it.

254
00:20:28,433 --> 00:20:29,000
Me too.

255
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,333
Seeing you

256
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,000
makes me happy.

257
00:20:54,467 --> 00:20:55,367
That girl...

258
00:20:56,567 --> 00:20:58,567
She's gentle and soft-spoken,

259
00:20:58,567 --> 00:21:00,300
and kind. A good person.

260
00:21:01,867 --> 00:21:02,900
Hayama,

261
00:21:03,833 --> 00:21:05,767
aren't you going to get a girlfriend?

262
00:21:13,933 --> 00:21:14,667
Of course,

263
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:16,767
he could get a girlfriend if he wanted.

264
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:32,567
I hate that.

265
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,467
I hate that.

266
00:21:47,833 --> 00:21:48,567
♪

267
00:21:52,067 --> 00:21:54,833
♪

268
00:21:55,133 --> 00:21:56,933
♪

269
00:21:58,233 --> 00:22:01,867
♪

270
00:22:02,067 --> 00:22:05,967
♪

271
00:22:10,367 --> 00:22:11,367
Hello?

272
00:22:12,667 --> 00:22:15,067
Want to grab a meal today?

273
